BUNDLED RECORDINGS (Salah/Resources/Audio/)

The app plays these recordings for adhan alerts and the optional du'a after the adhan.
All seven came into this code base with the app it was rebuilt from, Guidance for Mac
by Batoul Apps, where they were added in that repository's first commit (4de9e46,
24 October 2019). That repository has no license file, and nothing in it names the
recordings' original sources, performers' permissions or distribution terms.

  File                 Shown in the app as   Source                          License
  Adhan-Alafasy.m4a    Mishary Alafasy       Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unknown
  Adhan-Aqsa.mp3       Al-Aqsa               Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unknown
  Adhan-Fajr.mp3       Fajr Adhan            Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unknown
  Adhan-Istanbul.mp3   Istanbul              Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unknown
  Adhan-Makkah.mp3     Makkah                Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unknown
  Adhan-Yusuf.mp3      Yusuf Islam           Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unknown
  Dua.m4a              (du'a after adhan)    Guidance for Mac (Batoul Apps)  Unknown

Adhan-Alafasy.m4a is a recording of the adhan by Mishary Rashid Alafasy, a third-party
recording. Adhan-Yusuf.mp3 is presented as Yusuf Islam's adhan.

Open question: the right to redistribute these recordings, Adhan-Alafasy.m4a in
particular, has not been confirmed. Confirm it with the rights holders, or replace the
recordings with ones whose terms are clear, before any App Store or other binary
release. The MIT License of this repository does not cover them.


